+*   **When Not to Use:** Not suitable for scenes with strong specular reflections or heavy occlusion without additional filtering mechanisms [S1].
 
 ## Background
-OD-NeRF was introduced in the paper "OD-NeRF: Efficient Training of On-the-Fly Dynamic Neural Radiance Fields" [S1]. It addresses the challenge of efficient on-the-fly training where the radiance field is trained and rendered frame-by-frame. The method builds on the observation that projected colors of corresponding 3D points remain relatively invariant across consecutive frames, allowing the model to implicitly track correspondence without explicit temporal deformation [S1]. It is implemented on top of TiNeuVox for synthetic datasets and InstantNGP (via NerfAcc) for real-world datasets [S1].
+OD-NeRF was introduced in the paper "OD-NeRF: Efficient Training of On-the-Fly Dynamic Neural Radiance Fields" [S1]. The method addresses the challenge of efficiently utilizing radiance fields estimated from previous frames for on-the-fly training, a setting where the scene is captured and rendered sequentially. It builds on the spatial representations of TiNeuVox and InstantNGP but replaces temporal conditioning with projected color guidance [S1].
 
